{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CaBLt8WCPMWg56NvDFVrEw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017gU8FD8Vt8xd8LCd5Gou7b","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form soundness excitement overall score scale 2025","allowed_domains":["aclrollingreview.org"]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1005,"cache_read_input_tokens":50696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1005},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b38b24c5-912c-4a28-9ffb-691a58265a42","uuid":"9e44e574-dfac-4aee-8968-f1ca6788ad29"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017gU8FD8Vt8xd8LCd5Gou7b","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form soundness excitement overall score scale 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Changelog – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"http://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) review form and the three scoring dimensions for 2025:\n\n## Three Scoring Dimensions\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Soundness Score\n\nThe soundness score assesses whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and includes consideration of the depth and/or breadth of research questions, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation. Soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\nThe soundness scale includes ratings like:\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\n## Excitement Score\n\nExcitement is subjective and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field. Subjective preferences are reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\nThe excitement scale includes ratings like:\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n\n## Overall Recommendation Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b38b24c5-912c-4a28-9ffb-691a58265a42","uuid":"59dfce0a-4b30-43d2-9940-011d7b934cb7","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:50:01.298Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form soundness excitement overall score scale 2025","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Cotp3hzqqFFN7jn58pS8u7","content":[{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ARR Changelog – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"ARR Dashboard","url":"http://stats.aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) review form and the three scoring dimensions for 2025:\n\n## Three Scoring Dimensions\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Soundness Score\n\nThe soundness score assesses whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and includes consideration of the depth and/or breadth of research questions, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation. Soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\nThe soundness scale includes ratings like:\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\n## Excitement Score\n\nExcitement is subjective and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field. Subjective preferences are reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\nThe excitement scale includes ratings like:\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n\n## Overall Recommendation Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact."],"durationSeconds":7.653347588999997}}
